  "important_limitations": [
    "Similarity scores are algorithm-specific and do not represent human-perceived similarity percentages.",
    "The gameplay footage is not a silhouette animation: even the best frames only approximate Bad Apple!!'s pure black/white shapes; frames are shown unmodified, so colours, HUD and text remain visible.",
    "Adaptive sampling stores a subset of frames; skipped frames are near-duplicates of stored ones and frames around the most promising candidates are decoded densely in refinement, but a frame that is unique and far from every promising candidate can still be missed.",
    "Uniform reference frames (e.g. all black) can only be matched by brightness/uniformity.",
    "Dark-world gameplay is predominantly dark, so large white shapes have fewer good candidates than dark ones.",
    "Semantic similarity was not computed in this run (disabled by configuration)."
